{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-22226-r4615204","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Puliyodarai (South Indian Tamarind Rice)","sourcePageId":22226,"sourceRevision":"4615204","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:38:31Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Puliyodarai%20(South%20Indian%20Tamarind%20Rice)&oldid=4615204","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:08.534Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Pan fried recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using fenugreek seed","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Side dish recipes","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1f70ea7c3b876f0b20935d23726e4f8ad7af878f853b06a89afe2c1a00a9f385","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Rice recipes|servings=5|time=20 minutes|difficulty=2}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian Cuisine]]\n\n'''Puliyodarai''', is a speciality of the South [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian]] coastal state of [[w:Tamil Nadu|Tamil Nadu]].\n\n''Also see [[Cookbook:Pulihora]].''\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Garnishing powder ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Split Pea|split peas]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seeds\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Fenugreek|fenugreek]] seeds\n* 2–3 dry red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]]\n\n===Puliyodarai===\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] cooked white [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard seeds]]\n* 3 tbsp gingely ([[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame]]) oil (\"Til\" oil in Hindi, \"Nallennai\" in Tamil)\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Split Pea|split peas]]\n* 2 tbsp groundnuts ([[Cookbook:Peanut|peanuts]])\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]] (''heengh'' in Hindi, ''perungayum'' in Tamil)\n* 3–4 dry red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]]\n* 4–5 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 1.5 tbsp [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] concentrate\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* ¾ tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n===Garnishing Powder===\n# Dry roast all ingredients in a pan without oil until deep brown.\n# Grind to a fine powder after the mix cools down.\n\n===Puliyodarai===\n# Heat the oil in a pan.\n# Add groundnuts and split-peas, and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] until golden brown.\n# Add mustard seeds, asafoetida and red-chillies (broken into pieces). Wait until the mustard seeds splutter, then remove pan from stove.\n# Mix rice, salt, turmeric powder and tamarind concentrate. Add a little oil to the raw rice before cooking it. This gives it a better texture.\n# Add the garnishing powder and curry leaves and mix well.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* Serve with [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]]/curd.\n* Garnishing powder can be prepared ahead of time and can be stored for up to 2 months (no refrigeration needed).\n* Vary amount of salt/spices as needed.\n* 1 tsp sesame can be powdered and added for more taste.\n*A pinch of [[Cookbook:Jaggery|jaggery]] can be added\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fenugreek seed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Puliyodarai (South Indian Tamarind Rice)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tbsp split peas","sourceText":"1 tbsp split peas","amountText":"1 tbsp split peas","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tbsp coriander seeds","sourceText":"1 tbsp coriander seeds","amountText":"1 tbsp coriander seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ tsp fenugreek seeds","sourceText":"½ tsp fenugreek seeds","amountText":"½ tsp fenugreek seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2–3 dry red chillies","sourceText":"2–3 dry red chillies","amountText":"2–3 dry red chillies","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"4 cups cooked white rice","sourceText":"4 cups cooked white rice","amountText":"4 cups cooked white rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Vegetable oil","sourceText":"Vegetable oil","amountText":"Vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tsp mustard seeds","sourceText":"2 tsp mustard seeds","amountText":"2 tsp mustard seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"3 tbsp gingely (sesame) oil (\"Til\" oil in Hindi, \"Nallennai\" in Tamil)","sourceText":"3 tbsp gingely (sesame) oil (\"Til\" oil in Hindi, \"Nallennai\" in Tamil)","amountText